g to this dap  okay then somebody comes along and says  i want to send one ether to the address  of this dap why you want to do that  we'll see in just a minute but suppose  the user decides i want to send one  ether to this damp  well so again they issue a transaction a  miner and the trans a miner adds the  transa validated transaction as the  transaction to a block and post it to  the to the ethereum blockchain and then  what happens is basically the code of  the of the dap never changes this is  fixed forever but the state of the dap  now has changed in particular we record  that the value of the dap address is now  worth one ether okay so  what just happened here is that the user  sort of  sent a request to the program the dap  as a result of this request there was  code being executed in the dapp that  code moved the dap to a new state and  added value to the dap address okay so  people often ask well where is this code  running exactly and the answer is the  code was run by the miner who actually  created the block that contains this  transaction okay so the miner ran the  code  wrote the transaction that contains now  the new state of the dap  and  wrote that transaction to the blockchain  okay more more precisely the miner  actually verifies that the state was  computed correctly and in fact not just  that miner verifies it presumably all  the miners in the network verify that  the state is what it's supposed to be so  state one  of the dap is in fact what it is  supposed to be after receiving this  message from the user okay very good so  now the dap transitions to a new state  and again you realize the code in the  dap is the one that governed the  evolution of the of the state of the dap  the next thing that happens let's say  some other user issues another  transaction to the dap address so what  happens now is again the same thing the  code runs  and again what who runs it well the  miners basically verify that the  transaction  follow was constructed 